"id":"werk-kill-compare","kind":"card","title":"The from-scratch v0 is compared with the prototype by running the same user paths on both","why":"The kill criterion of #werk-base says 'too far from the prototype's behaviour' but names no measure. A shared set of user paths makes the distance a count.","body":"The kill criterion of #werk-base is measured by running the prototype's browser test paths against v0. The prototype's own browser tests are the reference paths, because they already pass on the prototype. A path that passes on the prototype and fails on v0 is one measured gap. The count of such gaps is the distance from the prototype's behaviour. A gap is first a missing or unclear card, not a reason to copy prototype code.","who":"me","status":"open"
